\ A word parameter declared fixnum/float is narrowed to an unboxed scalar at
\ codegen entry, so arithmetic and comparison on it compile to the concrete
\ path with no polymorphic fallback. Without the annotation these operate on
\ opaque parameters and each emits a per-op-native (arithmetic) or native
\ (comparison) fallback; with it, the stats below carry no such site. The only
\ remaining fallbacks are the `.` -> inspect prints, which narrowing does not
\ touch.

add2: ( a: fixnum b: fixnum -- r ) [ + ] ;
sub2: ( a: fixnum b: fixnum -- r ) [ - ] ;
mul2: ( a: fixnum b: fixnum -- r ) [ * ] ;
lt2:  ( a: fixnum b: fixnum -- r ) [ < ] ;
fadd: ( a: float b: float -- r )   [ + ] ;

3 4 add2 .
10 4 sub2 .
5 6 mul2 .
3 4 lt2 .
1.5 2.5 fadd .
